  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Access your Western Digital (WD) My Cloud device by signing in at MyCloud.com or by opening the My Cloud app on your phone. For desktop access, locate the device in Windows Explorer or macOS Finder. For cloud storage like iCloud, use iCloud.com or the Windows/Mac app. MyCloud.com iCloud.com Ways to Access Your Cloud Data Web Portal: Go to MyCloud.com and log in with your account credentials. MyCloud.com Mobile App: Download the My Cloud app on your smartphone to view, upload, and share files. Desktop (Windows/Mac): In File Explorer or Finder, your network-connected My Cloud device will appear in the network section, allowing you to open it like a local drive. Local Access (LAN): Use the URL http://mycloud-xxxxxx (replacing 'xxxxxx' with the last six digits of the serial number) to access the dashboard if you are on the same network. Accessing Other Common Cloud Services iCloud: Access from any browser at iCloud.com or through the iCloud app on Windows. iCloud.com Google Drive/Other: Use the specific desktop app (like Google Drive for Desktop) or visit the service’s website to log in. If you are experiencing issues with local access, try connecting the device directly to your computer's Ethernet port. This video demonstrates how to access the My Cloud Home dashboard using your device's hostname on a Mac:59sWDSupportChannelYouTube• Apr 7, 2023 59s",
